course: dictionary
lesson: 2818
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Disturb is a good example. «Do not disturb» on a hotel door means please don't interrupt, but a gust of wind can also disturb the leaves, which means it moves them.
explain: Read the words around disturb to decide. If someone is sleeping or busy, disturb means interrupt them. If the sentence is about a nest, a pond or a pile of rocks, disturb means move or upset something that was settled. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits.
explain: Disturbing is a related word, used for things that make us upset or uneasy. Disturb, disturbs, disturbed and disturbing all come from the same root, so once you know one form, you can work out the others.
fact: Disturb is a verb: disturb, disturbs, disturbed, disturbing.
fact: «Disturb» can mean to interrupt someone who is busy, resting or sleeping.
fact: «Disturb» can also mean to move something or change its position or order.
fact: «Disturbing» describes something that makes you upset or uneasy.
fact: «Poppies grow in disturbed soil», meaning soil that has been dug up or moved.
exercise: «Do not disturb» is on the hotel door. What does disturb mean here? | *Interrupt someone who is resting | Clean the room | Make a loud noise on purpose | Move the furniture
exercise: «Disturbing a nest makes wasps or bees attack in large numbers.» What does disturbing mean here? | Building a new nest | Watching it quietly | Singing near the nest | *Moving or upsetting the nest
exercise: Ali says «a disturbing noise» means a happy, cheerful noise. What does disturbing mean? | Sleepy and calm | Very quiet and soft | Cheerful and happy | *Upsetting or making you feel uneasy
test: «Please do not disturb the rock pool creatures.» What does disturb mean here? | Sing to them | Count them | *Move them or upset them | Make them sleep
test: Which form of disturb shows something that happened in the past? | *disturbed | disturbing | disturb | disturbs
exam: Pick the correct meaning: «The noise from the building site disturbed my sleep.» | Made my bed | Helped me sleep | *Interrupted my sleep | Painted my room
